# FastAPI Backend

- Prefer the existing project split: `routers/`, `services/`, `models/`, `schemas/`.
- Keep route handlers thin; move extraction, orchestration, and side effects into services.
- Use typed request/response models and explicit return shapes.
- Reuse FastAPI dependency injection for DB/session/settings/current user.
- Keep SQLAlchemy writes transactional and avoid opening ad hoc DB connections when a session already exists.
- For long-running or external work, log start/end/failure with structured fields.
- For this project, preserve the existing startup/lifespan pattern in `main.py`; do not introduce alternate app entrypoints casually.
- Follow existing security/auth patterns and do not weaken role checks or token handling.
